IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Work Health and Safety Regulations 2011 (Commonwealth) -- Chapter 8A (crystalline silica and the engineered stone
-- prohibition), with the regulations Chapter 8A sends the worker to: reg 50 (air monitoring), Part 7.1 Division 6
-- (health monitoring) and Schedule 14 item 7, Part 11.2 Division 3A (exemptions, reg 689A(2) only) and Part 8A of
-- Chapter 15 (the transitional regs 698A, 698B).
--
-- SEAT: the worker -- the person who cut, installed, removed or worked near crystalline silica or engineered stone for
-- a business or undertaking the Commonwealth Act covers. "Was my employer allowed to have me do this engineered stone
-- work? Was my processing controlled? What had to be done for me because it was high risk? Must I be given health
-- monitoring, and how long must the records of my exposure be kept?" The duties are all on the person conducting the
-- business or undertaking (the PCBU); they are encoded for what they mean to the worker.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 28, compilation date 25 March 2025 (register id F2025C00381), deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/F2011L02664.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19). Penalty amounts are those printed in Schedule 4
-- cl 2 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (C2024C00243), before indexation under cl 4.
--
-- Dates (NOTES.md finding 1): the Chapter came in by the Work Health and Safety Amendment (Penalties and Engineered
-- Stone and Crystalline Silica Substances) Regulations 2024 (F2024L00766): Sch 2 from 1 July 2024, Sch 3 from
-- 1 September 2024 (endnote 3). The endnotes do not say which Schedule inserted which regulation. This encoding takes
-- regs 529A to 529J other than 529CA to 529CE as in force from 1 July 2024, and regs 529CA to 529CE (the high-risk
-- duties) from 1 September 2024. Each is a fork line in NOTES.md.

§ `Work Health and Safety Regulations 2011, Chapter 8A -- the worker's questions`

`the engineered stone prohibition starts` MEANS Date 1 7 2024
`the high-risk processing duties start` MEANS Date 1 9 2024
-- reg 698A: the pre-2024-contract exception reaches contracts entered into on or before this day ...
`the last day for a pre-2024 contract to be entered into` MEANS Date 31 12 2023
-- ... for work carried out on or before this day.
`the last day of the pre-2024 contract exception` MEANS Date 31 12 2024

-- Periods of years. A period of N years beginning on a day ends on the day before the Nth anniversary of that day;
-- an anniversary that does not exist (29 February in a common year) is taken as 1 March, so the period ends on
-- 28 February. `Date` rolls an impossible date forward, which gives exactly that. A period "N years after" a day begins
-- on the next day (Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(1)), so callers add 1 first.
GIVEN `first day` IS A DATE
      `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of a period of years beginning on` IS
    (Date (DATE_DAY `first day`) (DATE_MONTH `first day`) (DATE_YEAR `first day` PLUS `years`)) MINUS 1

§§ `reg 529A -- what the material is, and what processing is`

-- reg 529A(2): "crystalline silica substance (CSS) means material that contains at least 1% crystalline silica,
-- determined as a weight/weight (w/w) concentration." (3): crystalline silica means crystalline polymorphs of silica,
-- including cristobalite, quartz, tridymite and tripoli. The percentage is a fact the worker can read off the product's
-- safety data sheet.
GIVEN `percent crystalline silica` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is a CSS` IF
    `percent crystalline silica` AT LEAST 1

@export Is the material I work with a "crystalline silica substance" (CSS) under the Work Health and Safety Regulations (reg 529A(2))?
GIVEN `percent crystalline silica` IS A NUMBER @desc The material's crystalline silica content (cristobalite, quartz, tridymite or tripoli) as a percentage by weight, for example 0.5 or 93, as the safety data sheet states it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the material a crystalline silica substance` IF
    `the material is a CSS` `percent crystalline silica`

-- reg 529A(4): "engineered stone: (a) means a CSS that: (i) is an artificial product; and (ii) is created by combining
-- natural stone materials with other chemical constituents such as water, resins or pigments; and (iii) becomes
-- hardened; but (b) does not include the following: (i) concrete and cement products; (ii) bricks, pavers and other
-- similar blocks; (iii) ceramic wall and floor tiles; (iv) grout, mortar and render; (v) plasterboard; (vi) porcelain
-- products; (vii) sintered stone; (viii) roof tiles."
-- reg 5: "porcelain product does not include a product that contains resin." "sintered stone does not include a product
-- that contains resin." So a porcelain or sintered product with resin in it is not excluded by (b)(vi) or (vii).
DECLARE `Product kind` IS ONE OF
    `a concrete or cement product`
    `a brick, paver or similar block`
    `a ceramic wall or floor tile`
    `grout, mortar or render`
    `plasterboard`
    `a porcelain product`
    `sintered stone`
    `a roof tile`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Product kind`
      `contains resin` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the product is excluded from engineered stone` IF
    CONSIDER `kind`
    WHEN `a porcelain product` THEN (NOT `contains resin`)
    WHEN `sintered stone` THEN (NOT `contains resin`)
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `percent crystalline silica` IS A NUMBER
      `artificial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `combines natural stone with other constituents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hardened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `kind` IS A `Product kind`
      `contains resin` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is engineered stone` IF
        `the material is a CSS` `percent crystalline silica`
    AND `artificial`
    AND `combines natural stone with other constituents`
    AND `hardened`
    AND (NOT (`the product is excluded from engineered stone` `kind` `contains resin`))

@export Is the stone product I work with "engineered stone" under the Work Health and Safety Regulations (reg 529A(4))?
GIVEN `percent crystalline silica` IS A NUMBER @desc The product's crystalline silica content as a percentage by weight, as its safety data sheet states it
      `artificial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the product is artificial (manufactured), not a natural stone quarried and cut
      `combines natural stone with other constituents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is made by combining natural stone materials (such as crushed quartz) with other chemical constituents such as water, resins or pigments
      `hardened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mixture then becomes hardened
      `kind` IS A `Product kind` @desc Which of these the product is, if any: a concrete or cement product; a brick, paver or similar block; a ceramic wall or floor tile; grout, mortar or render; plasterboard; a porcelain product; sintered stone; a roof tile; or none of these
      `contains resin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the product contains resin
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the product engineered stone` IF
    `the material is engineered stone` `percent crystalline silica` `artificial` `combines natural stone with other constituents` `hardened` `kind` `contains resin`

-- reg 529A(1): "processing in relation to a CSS means: (a) the use of power tools or mechanical plant to carry out an
-- activity involving the crushing, cutting, grinding, trimming, sanding, abrasive polishing or drilling of a CSS; or
-- (b) the use of roadheaders to excavate material that is a CSS; or (c) the quarrying of a material that is a CSS; or
-- (d) mechanical screening involving a material that is a CSS; or (e) tunnelling through a material that is a CSS; or
-- (f) a process that exposes, or is reasonably likely to expose, a person to respirable crystalline silica during the
-- manufacture or handling of a CSS." Whether (f) is "reasonably likely" is a judgment, asked as part of the choice.
DECLARE `Silica task` IS ONE OF
    `crushing, cutting, grinding, trimming, sanding, abrasive polishing or drilling it with power tools or mechanical plant`
    `excavating it with a roadheader`
    `quarrying it`
    `mechanical screening of it`
    `tunnelling through it`
    `manufacturing or handling it in a way that exposes, or is reasonably likely to expose, a person to respirable crystalline silica`
    `other work with it (for example handling by hand with no dust exposure likely)`

GIVEN `percent crystalline silica` IS A NUMBER
      `task` IS A `Silica task`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the task is processing of a CSS` IF
        `the material is a CSS` `percent crystalline silica`
    AND (NOT (`task` EQUALS `other work with it (for example handling by hand with no dust exposure likely)`))

@export Is what I do with this material "processing" of a crystalline silica substance under the Work Health and Safety Regulations (reg 529A(1))?
GIVEN `percent crystalline silica` IS A NUMBER @desc The material's crystalline silica content as a percentage by weight, as its safety data sheet states it
      `task` IS A `Silica task` @desc What I do with the material: power-tool or mechanical-plant crushing, cutting, grinding, trimming, sanding, abrasive polishing or drilling; roadheader excavation; quarrying; mechanical screening; tunnelling; manufacturing or handling that exposes or is reasonably likely to expose a person to respirable crystalline silica; or other work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my task processing of a crystalline silica substance` IF
    `the task is processing of a CSS` `percent crystalline silica` `task`

§§ `reg 529B -- when processing is controlled`

-- reg 529B(1): processing is controlled if "(a) control measures to eliminate or minimise risks arising from the
-- processing are implemented so far as is reasonably practicable; and (b) at least 1 of the following measures are used
-- during the processing: (i) the isolation of a person from dust exposure; (ii) a fully enclosed operator cabin fitted
-- with a high efficiency air filtration system; (iii) an effective wet dust suppression method; (iv) an effective
-- on-tool extraction system; (v) an effective local exhaust ventilation system; and (c) a person still at risk of being
-- exposed to respirable crystalline silica after 1 or more of the measures in paragraph (b) are used: (i) is provided
-- with respiratory protective equipment; and (ii) wears the respiratory protective equipment while the work is carried
-- out." (2): "Despite subregulation (1), if the measures in paragraph (1)(b) are not reasonably practicable, the
-- processing of a CSS is controlled if a person who is at risk of being exposed ... (a) is provided with respiratory
-- protective equipment; and (b) wears the respiratory protective equipment while the work is carried out."
-- (3): respiratory protective equipment means PPE designed to prevent the wearer inhaling airborne contaminants that
-- complies with AS/NZS 1716:2012 and AS/NZS 1715:2009.
-- "So far as is reasonably practicable" and "not reasonably practicable" are the court's weighing (Act s 18): asked as
-- inputs, never computed.
DECLARE `Controls used` HAS
    `risk control measures implemented so far as is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an engineering measure was used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `engineering measures were not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was still at risk of exposure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was given a respirator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the respirator meets AS/NZS 1716 and 1715` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I wore it while the work was done` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A `Controls used`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `respiratory protective equipment was provided and worn` IF
        `c`'s `I was given a respirator`
    AND `c`'s `the respirator meets AS/NZS 1716 and 1715`
    AND `c`'s `I wore it while the work was done`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Controls used`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the processing is controlled` IF
        (    `c`'s `risk control measures implemented so far as is reasonably practicable`
         AND `c`'s `an engineering measure was used`
         AND (    (NOT (`c`'s `I was still at risk of exposure`))
              OR `respiratory protective equipment was provided and worn` `c`))
    OR  (    `c`'s `engineering measures were not reasonably practicable`
         AND `respiratory protective equipment was provided and worn` `c`)

@export Was the processing I did "controlled" under the Work Health and Safety Regulations (reg 529B)?
GIVEN `risk control measures implemented so far as is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether control measures to eliminate or minimise the risks of the processing were implemented so far as is reasonably practicable (if a court would find so)
      `an engineering measure was used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one of these was used during the processing: isolation from the dust; a fully enclosed operator cabin with high efficiency air filtration; effective wet dust suppression; effective on-tool extraction; effective local exhaust ventilation
      `engineering measures were not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether none of those five measures was reasonably practicable for this processing (if a court would find so)
      `I was still at risk of exposure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether I was still at risk of breathing respirable crystalline silica after the measures used
      `I was given a respirator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business gave me respiratory protective equipment
      `the respirator meets AS/NZS 1716 and 1715` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that equipment complies with AS/NZS 1716:2012 and AS/NZS 1715:2009
      `I wore it while the work was done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether I wore it while the work was carried out
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my processing controlled` IF
    `the processing is controlled` (`Controls used` WITH
        `risk control measures implemented so far as is reasonably practicable` IS `risk control measures implemented so far as is reasonably practicable`
        `an engineering measure was used` IS `an engineering measure was used`
        `engineering measures were not reasonably practicable` IS `engineering measures were not reasonably practicable`
        `I was still at risk of exposure` IS `I was still at risk of exposure`
        `I was given a respirator` IS `I was given a respirator`
        `the respirator meets AS/NZS 1716 and 1715` IS `the respirator meets AS/NZS 1716 and 1715`
        `I wore it while the work was done` IS `I wore it while the work was done`)

§§ `reg 529C -- processing must be controlled`

-- reg 529C: "A person conducting a business or undertaking must not carry out, or direct or allow a worker to carry
-- out, processing of a CSS unless the processing is controlled." Penalty: the tier E monetary penalty.
-- A flat prohibition with "unless": JUST FALSE once the processing is controlled (ruling N2 and the case-by-case rule
-- for "unless", fork line F3). Before 1 July 2024 the regulation was not in force: NOTHING (the Regulations are silent).
GIVEN `day of the work` IS A DATE
      `percent crystalline silica` IS A NUMBER
      `task` IS A `Silica task`
      `controlled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 529C was breached` IS
    IF `day of the work` LESS THAN `the engineered stone prohibition starts`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT (`the task is processing of a CSS` `percent crystalline silica` `task`)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (NOT `controlled`)

@export Did my employer break the rule that processing of crystalline silica must be controlled, on the day I did the work (reg 529C)? No answer means the rule did not reach the work (before 1 July 2024, or not processing of a CSS).
GIVEN `day of the work` IS A DATE @desc The day I did the work
      `percent crystalline silica` IS A NUMBER @desc The material's crystalline silica content as a percentage by weight
      `task` IS A `Silica task` @desc What I did with the material (see the processing question)
      `controlled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the processing was controlled (the answer to the reg 529B question)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my employer let me process silica uncontrolled` IS
    `reg 529C was breached` `day of the work` `percent crystalline silica` `task` `controlled`

§§ `regs 529D to 529F, 689A, 698A -- the engineered stone prohibition`

-- reg 529D: "A person conducting a business or undertaking must not carry out, or direct or allow a worker to carry
-- out, work that involves manufacturing, supplying, processing or installing engineered stone benchtops, panels or
-- slabs." Penalty: the tier E monetary penalty.
-- reg 529E: 529D "does not apply to work that involves supplying or installing engineered stone benchtops, panels or
-- slabs if the work is: (a) for genuine research and analysis; or (b) to sample and identify engineered stone."
-- reg 529F: 529D "does not apply to work that involves processing engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs if the
-- work: (a) is carried out: (i) for genuine research and analysis; or (ii) to sample and identify engineered stone; or
-- (iii) to remove, repair or make minor modifications to installed engineered stone; or (iv) to dispose of the
-- engineered stone, whether it is installed or not; and (b) is controlled."
-- reg 689A(2): the PCBU "is exempt from compliance with regulation 529D if the work involves a type of engineered stone
-- that is the subject of an exemption granted under: (a) subregulation (1); or (b) a corresponding WHS law that is
-- equivalent to subregulation (1)." Whether an exemption was granted is a fact the worker asks the regulator.
-- reg 698A(1): 529D "does not apply to work that involves installing engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs if:
-- (a) the work is carried out: (i) under a contract originally entered into on or before 31 December 2023; and (ii) on
-- or before 31 December 2024 in a place to which a corresponding WHS law applies; and (b) if the corresponding WHS law
-- applied to the work, regulation 529D of the corresponding WHS law would not apply to the work under that law because
-- the work was carried out on or before 31 December 2024." (2): the same for supplying or processing for installation
-- under such a contract, "(d) for work that involves processing the engineered stone -- the processing is controlled."
-- Conditions (a)(ii) and (b) of (1) and (b) and (c) of (2) are asked together as one fact (NOTES.md finding 4).
-- reg 698B (acquisition of property otherwise than on just terms) is a constitutional question for a court: out.
DECLARE `Stone work` IS ONE OF
    `manufacturing`
    `supplying`
    `processing`
    `installing`

DECLARE `Stone work purpose` IS ONE OF
    `genuine research and analysis`
    `sampling and identifying engineered stone`
    `removing, repairing or making minor modifications to installed engineered stone`
    `disposing of the engineered stone`
    `ordinary work (making, fitting or selling benchtops, panels or slabs)`

DECLARE `Stone work facts` HAS
    `day of the work` IS A DATE
    `work` IS A `Stone work`
    `it is a benchtop, panel or slab` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose` IS A `Stone work purpose`
    `controlled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this type of engineered stone is exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contract entered into on` IS A DATE
    `the State or Territory transition also covered it` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Prohibition answer` IS ONE OF
    `the prohibition was not yet in force (before 1 July 2024)`
    `not engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs: reg 529D does not reach it`
    `allowed: the type of engineered stone is exempted (reg 689A)`
    `allowed: research or sampling (reg 529E)`
    `allowed: research, sampling, removal, repair, minor modification or disposal, and controlled (reg 529F)`
    `allowed: work under a contract entered into by 31 December 2023 (reg 698A)`
    `prohibited (reg 529D)`

GIVEN `f` IS A `Stone work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 529E applies` IF
        (`f`'s `work` EQUALS `supplying` OR `f`'s `work` EQUALS `installing`)
    AND (   `f`'s `purpose` EQUALS `genuine research and analysis`
         OR `f`'s `purpose` EQUALS `sampling and identifying engineered stone`)

GIVEN `f` IS A `Stone work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 529F applies` IF
        `f`'s `work` EQUALS `processing`
    AND (NOT (`f`'s `purpose` EQUALS `ordinary work (making, fitting or selling benchtops, panels or slabs)`))
    AND `f`'s `controlled`

GIVEN `f` IS A `Stone work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 698A applies` IF
        `f`'s `contract entered into on` AT MOST `the last day for a pre-2024 contract to be entered into`
    AND `f`'s `day of the work` AT MOST `the last day of the pre-2024 contract exception`
    AND `f`'s `the State or Territory transition also covered it`
    AND (   `f`'s `work` EQUALS `installing`
         OR `f`'s `work` EQUALS `supplying`
         OR (`f`'s `work` EQUALS `processing` AND `f`'s `controlled`))

GIVEN `f` IS A `Stone work facts`
GIVETH A `Prohibition answer`
DECIDE `what reg 529D says` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `f`'s `day of the work` LESS THAN `the engineered stone prohibition starts`
            THEN `the prohibition was not yet in force (before 1 July 2024)`
        IF NOT (`f`'s `it is a benchtop, panel or slab`)
            THEN `not engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs: reg 529D does not reach it`
        IF `f`'s `this type of engineered stone is exempted`
            THEN `allowed: the type of engineered stone is exempted (reg 689A)`
        IF `reg 529E applies` `f`
            THEN `allowed: research or sampling (reg 529E)`
        IF `reg 529F applies` `f`
            THEN `allowed: research, sampling, removal, repair, minor modification or disposal, and controlled (reg 529F)`
        IF `reg 698A applies` `f`
            THEN `allowed: work under a contract entered into by 31 December 2023 (reg 698A)`
        OTHERWISE `prohibited (reg 529D)`

@export Was my employer allowed to have me do this work with engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs on that day, or did the engineered stone ban forbid it (regs 529D to 529F, 689A, 698A)?
GIVEN `day of the work` IS A DATE @desc The day I did the work
      `work` IS A `Stone work` @desc What the work was: manufacturing, supplying, processing (cutting, grinding, polishing and the like) or installing
      `it is a benchtop, panel or slab` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work was on engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs (use the engineered stone question first if unsure the product is engineered stone)
      `purpose` IS A `Stone work purpose` @desc Why the work was done: genuine research and analysis; sampling and identifying engineered stone; removing, repairing or making minor modifications to installed engineered stone; disposing of it; or ordinary work
      `controlled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the processing was controlled (the answer to the reg 529B question); answer no if there was no processing
      `this type of engineered stone is exempted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulator (or a State or Territory regulator under an equivalent law) has exempted this type of engineered stone from the ban
      `contract entered into on` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract for the job was originally entered into
      `the State or Territory transition also covered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work was done in a place where a State or Territory WHS law applies and that law's own ban would not have applied to it because it was done by 31 December 2024
GIVETH A `Prohibition answer`
DECIDE `What does the engineered stone ban say about my work` IS
    `what reg 529D says` (`Stone work facts` WITH
        `day of the work` IS `day of the work`
        `work` IS `work`
        `it is a benchtop, panel or slab` IS `it is a benchtop, panel or slab`
        `purpose` IS `purpose`
        `controlled` IS `controlled`
        `this type of engineered stone is exempted` IS `this type of engineered stone is exempted`
        `contract entered into on` IS `contract entered into on`
        `the State or Territory transition also covered it` IS `the State or Territory transition also covered it`)

-- reg 529G(2): "Before the work is carried out", a PCBU carrying out, or directing or allowing a worker to carry out,
-- processing of engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs "(a) to remove, repair or make minor modifications to
-- installed engineered stone; or (b) to dispose of the engineered stone" must give the regulator a written notice.
-- (3): not if the PCBU "does not know, and could not reasonably be expected to know, before the work is carried out" that
-- it involves processing engineered stone, and gives the notice "as soon as practicable" after becoming aware.
-- Penalty: the tier G monetary penalty.
DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `no notice is required for this work`
    `notice was required before the work started`
    `notice was required as soon as practicable after the business became aware`

GIVEN `day of the work` IS A DATE
      `work` IS A `Stone work`
      `purpose` IS A `Stone work purpose`
      `the business could have known beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `what reg 529G requires` IS
    IF     `day of the work` AT LEAST `the engineered stone prohibition starts`
       AND `work` EQUALS `processing`
       AND (   `purpose` EQUALS `removing, repairing or making minor modifications to installed engineered stone`
            OR `purpose` EQUALS `disposing of the engineered stone`)
    THEN IF `the business could have known beforehand`
         THEN `notice was required before the work started`
         ELSE `notice was required as soon as practicable after the business became aware`
    ELSE `no notice is required for this work`

@export Did my employer have to notify the regulator of the engineered stone removal, repair, modification or disposal work I did, and when (reg 529G)?
GIVEN `day of the work` IS A DATE @desc The day the work was carried out
      `work` IS A `Stone work` @desc What the work was: manufacturing, supplying, processing or installing
      `purpose` IS A `Stone work purpose` @desc Why the work was done (removal, repair or minor modification of installed engineered stone, disposal, research, sampling, or ordinary work)
      `the business could have known beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business knew, or could reasonably be expected to have known, before the work started that it involved processing engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `Must my employer notify the regulator of this engineered stone work` IS
    `what reg 529G requires` `day of the work` `work` `purpose` `the business could have known beforehand`

-- reg 529H(1): if the notified information changes, the PCBU must "within the period ending 30 days after the day the
-- change occurs" give the regulator a written notice. reg 529I(1)-(2): if 12 months "beginning on the day the last
-- notice is given about the work" end and the work is still being carried out, the PCBU must "within the period of 30
-- days ending after the day the 12-month period ends" give a further notice (NOTES.md finding 3 on the wording).
-- A period of 12 months beginning on a day ends on the day before its anniversary.
GIVEN `day of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day for a change notice` IS
    `day of the change` PLUS 30

GIVEN `day the last notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of the 12-month period` IS
    `the last day of a period of years beginning on` `day the last notice was given` 1

GIVEN `day the last notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day for a continuing-work notice` IS
    `the last day of the 12-month period` `day the last notice was given` PLUS 30

@export The engineered stone work I do has been notified to the regulator and is still going on. By what day must my employer tell the regulator it continues (reg 529I)?
GIVEN `day the last notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the business last gave the regulator a notice about this work
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must my employer notify that the engineered stone work continues` IS
    `the last day for a continuing-work notice` `day the last notice was given`

@export Something in my employer's engineered stone notice to the regulator has changed. By what day must my employer notify the change (reg 529H)?
GIVEN `day of the change` IS A DATE @desc The day the notified information changed
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must my employer notify a change in the engineered stone work` IS
    `the last day for a change notice` `day of the change`

-- reg 529J: the PCBU must, "for a period of 5 years beginning on the day the notice is given to the regulator: (a) keep a
-- copy of the notice; and (b) ensure that a copy of the notice is readily accessible; and (c) allow a person to access a
-- copy of the notice upon request." Penalty: the tier G monetary penalty.
GIVEN `day the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day the notice must be kept` IS
    `the last day of a period of years beginning on` `day the notice was given` 5

@export Until what day can I ask my employer to let me see the engineered stone notice it gave the regulator (reg 529J)?
GIVEN `day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the business gave the notice to the regulator
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when can I see my employer's engineered stone notice` IS
    `the last day the notice must be kept` `day the notice was given`

§§ `regs 529CA to 529CE -- processing that is high risk (from 1 September 2024)`

-- reg 529CA(1): the PCBU "must assess the processing of a CSS ... to determine if the processing is high risk"; (4) the
-- assessment must be recorded in writing. (5): "If a person conducting a business or undertaking is unable to determine
-- whether the processing of a CSS carried out at the workplace is high risk, the processing is taken to be high risk
-- until the person determines that the processing is not high risk." Where no assessment was made at all, the text does
-- not say what follows for the processing: NOTHING (fork line F5); the failure to assess is itself a breach of (1).
DECLARE `High risk assessment` IS ONE OF
    `assessed as high risk`
    `assessed as not high risk`
    `the business could not determine whether it is high risk`
    `no assessment was made`

GIVEN `assessment` IS A `High risk assessment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the processing is high risk` IS
    CONSIDER `assessment`
    WHEN `assessed as high risk` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `assessed as not high risk` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the business could not determine whether it is high risk` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `no assessment was made` THEN NOTHING

@export Is the silica processing I do treated as "high risk" under the Work Health and Safety Regulations (reg 529CA)? No answer means the business made no assessment, which the text does not resolve.
GIVEN `assessment` IS A `High risk assessment` @desc What the business's written risk assessment found: high risk; not high risk; could not determine; or no assessment was made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my silica processing high risk` IS
    `the processing is high risk` `assessment`

-- What the business must do once processing is high risk:
-- reg 529CB(1): ensure, "before the processing commences", that a silica risk control plan is prepared (or has been by
-- another person); (3): not required if the processing is also high risk construction work and a safe work method
-- statement meeting (2) is prepared before it commences.
-- reg 529CC(1): ensure the plan is "(a) available to all workers; and (b) provided to all workers before they commence
-- the processing"; (2): processing not in accordance with the plan must be "stopped immediately or as soon as it is safe
-- to do so" and resumed only in accordance with the plan.
-- reg 529CD(1): crystalline silica training for a worker the PCBU "reasonably believes ... may be: (a) involved in the
-- processing of a CSS that is high risk; or (b) at risk of exposure to respirable crystalline silica because of" it.
-- reg 529CE: "(a) undertake air monitoring for respirable crystalline silica in accordance with regulation 50; and ...
-- (c) provide health monitoring for all workers carrying out the processing of a CSS that is high risk".
DECLARE `High risk duty` IS ONE OF
    `prepare a silica risk control plan before the processing starts (reg 529CB)`
    `prepare a safe work method statement meeting reg 529CB(2) before the processing starts (reg 529CB(3))`
    `make the plan available to me and give it to me before I start the processing (reg 529CC(1))`
    `stop the processing if it departs from the plan, and resume only in accordance with it (reg 529CC(2))`
    `give me accredited or approved crystalline silica training (reg 529CD)`
    `carry out air monitoring for respirable crystalline silica (reg 529CE(a), reg 50)`
    `give me health monitoring (reg 529CE(c), Part 7.1 Division 6)`

GIVEN `day of the work` IS A DATE
      `high risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I do the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I may be exposed by it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is high risk construction work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `High risk duty`
DECIDE `the high risk duties owed to me` IS
    IF (`day of the work` LESS THAN `the high-risk processing duties start`) OR (NOT `high risk`)
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `plan duty`
         FOLLOWED BY `make the plan available to me and give it to me before I start the processing (reg 529CC(1))`
         FOLLOWED BY `stop the processing if it departs from the plan, and resume only in accordance with it (reg 529CC(2))`
         FOLLOWED BY (append `training duty` `monitoring duties`)
    WHERE
        `plan duty` MEANS
            IF `it is high risk construction work`
            THEN `prepare a safe work method statement meeting reg 529CB(2) before the processing starts (reg 529CB(3))`
            ELSE `prepare a silica risk control plan before the processing starts (reg 529CB)`
        `training duty` MEANS
            IF `I do the processing` OR `I may be exposed by it`
            THEN LIST `give me accredited or approved crystalline silica training (reg 529CD)`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `monitoring duties` MEANS
            IF `I do the processing`
            THEN LIST `carry out air monitoring for respirable crystalline silica (reg 529CE(a), reg 50)`, `give me health monitoring (reg 529CE(c), Part 7.1 Division 6)`
            ELSE LIST `carry out air monitoring for respirable crystalline silica (reg 529CE(a), reg 50)`

@export My workplace's silica processing is high risk. What must my employer do for me because of it (regs 529CB to 529CE)?
GIVEN `day of the work` IS A DATE @desc The day of the work (these duties apply from 1 September 2024)
      `high risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the processing is high risk (the answer to the high-risk question)
      `I do the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether I carry out the processing myself
      `I may be exposed by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business reasonably believes I may be at risk of breathing respirable crystalline silica because of the processing, even if I do not do it
      `it is high risk construction work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the processing is also high risk construction work, covered by a safe work method statement
GIVETH A LIST OF `High risk duty`
DECIDE `What must my employer do because my silica processing is high risk` IS
    `the high risk duties owed to me` `day of the work` `high risk` `I do the processing` `I may be exposed by it` `it is high risk construction work`

-- reg 529CD(2): the record of the training must be kept "(a) while the worker is carrying out the processing of a CSS
-- that is high risk; and (b) for 5 years after the day the worker ceases working for the person." Penalty: tier I.
-- "5 years after the day": the period begins the next day (the day itself excluded, Acts Interpretation Act 1901
-- s 36(1)), so it ends on the fifth anniversary of the day (NOTES.md, method for periods).
GIVEN `day I stopped working for the business` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day the training record must be kept` IS
    `the last day of a period of years beginning on` (`day I stopped working for the business` PLUS 1) 5

@export Until what day must my former employer keep the record of my crystalline silica training (reg 529CD(2))?
GIVEN `day I stopped working for the business` IS A DATE @desc The day I stopped working for the business
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when must my silica training record be kept` IS
    `the last day the training record must be kept` `day I stopped working for the business`

-- reg 529CE(b): the PCBU must "provide air monitoring results to the regulator, in a form approved by the regulator, if
-- the airborne concentration of respirable crystalline silica has exceeded the workplace exposure standard as soon as
-- reasonably practicable and no more than 14 days from the date that the air monitoring result was reported to the
-- person". Where the standard was not exceeded there is no such duty: NOTHING (no deadline; fork line F6).
GIVEN `day the result was reported to the business` IS A DATE
      `the result exceeded the exposure standard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the last day to give the result to the regulator` IS
    IF     `the result exceeded the exposure standard`
       AND `day the result was reported to the business` AT LEAST `the high-risk processing duties start`
    THEN JUST (`day the result was reported to the business` PLUS 14)
    ELSE NOTHING

@export An air monitoring result at my workplace showed respirable crystalline silica over the exposure standard. By what day must my employer send it to the regulator (reg 529CE(b))? No answer means there is no such deadline.
GIVEN `day the result was reported to the business` IS A DATE @desc The day the air monitoring result was reported to the business
      `the result exceeded the exposure standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the airborne concentration of respirable crystalline silica exceeded the workplace exposure standard
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By when must my employer report the silica air monitoring result` IS
    `the last day to give the result to the regulator` `day the result was reported to the business` `the result exceeded the exposure standard`

-- reg 50(2): the results of air monitoring "are recorded, and kept for 30 years after the date the record is made";
-- (3): "readily accessible to persons at the workplace who may be exposed". Penalties: tier I and tier G.
GIVEN `day the record was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day an exposure record must be kept` IS
    `the last day of a period of years beginning on` (`day the record was made` PLUS 1) 30

@export Until what day must my employer keep the air monitoring record of the silica dust at my workplace (reg 50(2))?
GIVEN `day the record was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the air monitoring record was made
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when must the air monitoring record be kept` IS
    `the last day an exposure record must be kept` `day the record was made`

§§ `Part 7.1 Division 6, Schedule 14 item 7 -- health monitoring for crystalline silica`

-- reg 368: the PCBU "must ensure that health monitoring is provided to a worker ... if: (a) the worker is carrying out
-- ongoing work at a workplace using, handling, generating or storing hazardous chemicals and there is a significant risk
-- to the worker's health because of exposure to a hazardous chemical referred to in Schedule 14, table 14.1, column 2".
-- Crystalline silica is item 7 of table 14.1. "Significant risk" is a judgment, asked as an input. Penalty: tier E.
-- reg 529CE(c) adds health monitoring for every worker carrying out high-risk processing of a CSS, from 1 September 2024.
-- Both are "if" conditions: JUST FALSE / FALSE when neither holds.
GIVEN `day` IS A DATE
      `ongoing work with crystalline silica` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant risk to my health from it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I carry out high-risk processing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `health monitoring is owed to me` IF
        (`ongoing work with crystalline silica` AND `significant risk to my health from it`)
    OR  (`I carry out high-risk processing` AND `day` AT LEAST `the high-risk processing duties start`)

@export Must my employer provide me with health monitoring for crystalline silica, at its cost (regs 368, 372, 529CE(c))?
GIVEN `day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is asked about
      `ongoing work with crystalline silica` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether I carry out ongoing work using, handling, generating or storing crystalline silica
      `significant risk to my health from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a significant risk to my health because of exposure to respirable crystalline silica (as the business, and ultimately a court, would judge it)
      `I carry out high-risk processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether I carry out processing of a crystalline silica substance that is high risk (the answer to the high-risk question)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me silica health monitoring` IF
    `health monitoring is owed to me` `day` `ongoing work with crystalline silica` `significant risk to my health from it` `I carry out high-risk processing`

-- reg 370 and Schedule 14, table 14.1, item 7: for crystalline silica the health monitoring must include
-- "Demographic, medical and occupational history; Records of personal exposure; Standardised respiratory questionnaire to
-- be completed; Standardised respiratory function test, for example, FEV1, FVC and FEV1/FVC; Chest X-ray full size PA
-- view", unless "(a) an equal or better type of health monitoring is available; and (b) the use of that other type of
-- monitoring is recommended by a registered medical practitioner with experience in health monitoring".
-- reg 371(1): carried out by or under the supervision of such a practitioner; (2): the worker is consulted on the choice.
-- reg 372(1): the PCBU pays all expenses.
DECLARE `Health monitoring item` IS ONE OF
    `demographic, medical and occupational history`
    `records of personal exposure`
    `a standardised respiratory questionnaire`
    `a standardised respiratory function test (for example FEV1, FVC and FEV1/FVC)`
    `a full size PA chest X-ray`
    `an equal or better type of monitoring recommended by an experienced registered medical practitioner`

GIVEN `a doctor recommends an equal or better type` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Health monitoring item`
DECIDE `the health monitoring I must be given` IS
    IF `a doctor recommends an equal or better type`
    THEN LIST `an equal or better type of monitoring recommended by an experienced registered medical practitioner`
    ELSE LIST `demographic, medical and occupational history`, `records of personal exposure`, `a standardised respiratory questionnaire`, `a standardised respiratory function test (for example FEV1, FVC and FEV1/FVC)`, `a full size PA chest X-ray`

@export What must my crystalline silica health monitoring include (reg 370, Schedule 14 item 7)?
GIVEN `a doctor recommends an equal or better type` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an equal or better type of health monitoring is available and a registered medical practitioner experienced in health monitoring recommends using it instead
GIVETH A LIST OF `Health monitoring item`
DECIDE `What must my silica health monitoring include` IS
    `the health monitoring I must be given` `a doctor recommends an equal or better type`

-- reg 378(1): health monitoring reports are kept "as a confidential record: (a) identified as a record in relation to
-- the worker; and (b) for at least 30 years after the record is made." Penalty: tier I.
@export Until what day must my employer keep my health monitoring report (reg 378(1))?
GIVEN `day the record was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the health monitoring report was made
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when must my health monitoring report be kept` IS
    `the last day an exposure record must be kept` `day the record was made`

-- reg 378(2): the PCBU "must ensure that the health monitoring report and results of a worker are not disclosed to
-- another person without the worker's written consent." (3): "Subregulation (2) does not apply if the record is
-- disclosed under regulation 376 or 377 or to a person who must keep the record confidential under a duty of
-- professional confidentiality."
-- reg 376: to the regulator, if the report contains "(a) any advice that test results indicate that the worker may have
-- contracted a disease, injury or illness as a result of carrying out the work ...; or (b) any recommendation that the
-- person ... take remedial measures". reg 377: to all other PCBUs who have a duty to provide health monitoring for the
-- worker. A flat negative with a closed list of exceptions: JUST FALSE / FALSE outside them (ruling N2).
DECLARE `Report recipient` IS ONE OF
    `the regulator`
    `another business that must also provide me health monitoring`
    `a person bound by a duty of professional confidentiality`
    `anyone else (for example a new employer or an insurer)`

GIVEN `recipient` IS A `Report recipient`
      `the report advises a work-caused disease or recommends remedial measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report may be disclosed` IF
        `I gave written consent`
    OR  (`recipient` EQUALS `the regulator` AND `the report advises a work-caused disease or recommends remedial measures`)
    OR  `recipient` EQUALS `another business that must also provide me health monitoring`
    OR  `recipient` EQUALS `a person bound by a duty of professional confidentiality`

@export May my employer give my health monitoring report to this person (reg 378(2), (3), 376, 377)?
GIVEN `recipient` IS A `Report recipient` @desc Who would receive it: the regulator; another business that must also provide me health monitoring; a person bound by a duty of professional confidentiality; or anyone else
      `the report advises a work-caused disease or recommends remedial measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the report says test results indicate I may have contracted a disease, injury or illness from the work, or recommends the business take remedial measures
      `I gave written consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether I gave written consent to this disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my health monitoring report be disclosed` IF
    `the report may be disclosed` `recipient` `the report advises a work-caused disease or recommends remedial measures` `I gave written consent`

§§ `Penalties -- Act Schedule 4 cl 2, printed amounts before indexation`

-- Each offence regulation names a tier. Schedule 4 cl 2 of the Act: tier E $8,400 (individual) / $42,000 (body
-- corporate); tier G $5,000 / $25,000; tier I $1,700 / $8,500; "as indexed under clause 4 and rounded under clause 5".
-- Indexing is encoded in the Act's encoding (whs-penalty-indexation.l4); it cannot be imported from here (another
-- subject's folder), so these are the printed figures.
DECLARE `Silica duty breached` IS ONE OF
    `reg 529C: processing not controlled`
    `reg 529CA(1): no high-risk assessment`
    `reg 529CA(4): assessment not in writing`
    `reg 529CB(1): no silica risk control plan`
    `reg 529CC(1) or (2): plan not given to workers, or processing not stopped`
    `reg 529CC(3): plan not reviewed`
    `reg 529CD(1): no crystalline silica training`
    `reg 529CD(2) or (3): training record not kept or not available`
    `reg 529CE: no air or health monitoring, or result not reported`
    `reg 529D: prohibited engineered stone work`
    `regs 529G to 529J: engineered stone notice not given or kept`
    `reg 50(1): no air monitoring`
    `reg 50(2): air monitoring record not kept`
    `reg 50(3): air monitoring results not accessible`
    `reg 368, 370, 371(1), 374(1), 375, 376 or 377: health monitoring or its report`
    `reg 369, 371(2), 372(1) or 373: health monitoring information, consultation or cost`
    `reg 378: health monitoring record not kept or disclosed`

DECLARE `Penalty tier` IS ONE OF `tier E`, `tier G`, `tier I`

GIVEN `duty` IS A `Silica duty breached`
GIVETH A `Penalty tier`
DECIDE `the tier for` IS
    CONSIDER `duty`
    WHEN `reg 529CA(4): assessment not in writing` THEN `tier I`
    WHEN `reg 529CC(3): plan not reviewed` THEN `tier G`
    WHEN `reg 529CD(2) or (3): training record not kept or not available` THEN `tier I`
    WHEN `regs 529G to 529J: engineered stone notice not given or kept` THEN `tier G`
    WHEN `reg 50(2): air monitoring record not kept` THEN `tier I`
    WHEN `reg 50(3): air monitoring results not accessible` THEN `tier G`
    WHEN `reg 369, 371(2), 372(1) or 373: health monitoring information, consultation or cost` THEN `tier G`
    WHEN `reg 378: health monitoring record not kept or disclosed` THEN `tier I`
    OTHERWISE `tier E`

GIVEN `tier` IS A `Penalty tier`
      `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the printed amount for` IS
    CONSIDER `tier`
    WHEN `tier E` THEN IF `a body corporate` THEN 42000 ELSE 8400
    WHEN `tier G` THEN IF `a body corporate` THEN 25000 ELSE 5000
    WHEN `tier I` THEN IF `a body corporate` THEN 8500 ELSE 1700

@export What is the most my employer can be fined for breaching this silica or engineered stone duty (Act Schedule 4 cl 2, printed amount before indexation)?
GIVEN `duty` IS A `Silica duty breached` @desc Which duty the business broke
      `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business is a company or other body corporate (otherwise an individual)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my employer can be fined for this silica breach` IS
    `the printed amount for` (`the tier for` `duty`) `a body corporate`

§§ `The duties with deadlines, as regulative rules`

-- Time in these rules is counted in days from the day the duty arises (day 0). They are traced in the cases file; no
-- exported question takes one as an input.
DECLARE `Silica party` IS ONE OF
    `the business`
    `I, the worker`

DECLARE `Silica action` IS ONE OF
    `carry out, or direct or allow me to carry out, prohibited engineered stone work`
    `give the air monitoring result to the regulator`
    `notify the regulator of the change`
    `notify the regulator that the work continues`
    `obtain the health monitoring report`
    `give me a copy of the health monitoring report`

-- reg 529D, where none of regs 529E, 529F, 689A or 698A applies (the `prohibited (reg 529D)` answer above).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Silica party` `Silica action`
`the engineered stone prohibition` MEANS
    PARTY `the business`
    SHANT `carry out, or direct or allow me to carry out, prohibited engineered stone work`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the business` BECAUSE "reg 529D: a business must not carry out, or direct or allow a worker to carry out, work that involves manufacturing, supplying, processing or installing engineered stone benchtops, panels or slabs (tier E)"

-- reg 529CE(b): day 0 is the day the result over the exposure standard was reported to the business.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Silica party` `Silica action`
`the air monitoring reporting duty` MEANS
    PARTY  `the business`
    MUST   `give the air monitoring result to the regulator`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST   BREACH BY `the business` BECAUSE "reg 529CE(b): a result over the exposure standard must reach the regulator no more than 14 days from the day it was reported to the business (tier E)"

-- reg 529H(1): day 0 is the day the notified information changed.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Silica party` `Silica action`
`the change notice duty` MEANS
    PARTY  `the business`
    MUST   `notify the regulator of the change`
    WITHIN 30
    LEST   BREACH BY `the business` BECAUSE "reg 529H(1): a change in notified information must be notified within 30 days after the day of the change (tier G)"

-- reg 529I(2): day 0 is the last day of the 12-month period beginning on the day the last notice was given.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Silica party` `Silica action`
`the continuing-work notice duty` MEANS
    PARTY  `the business`
    MUST   `notify the regulator that the work continues`
    WITHIN 30
    LEST   BREACH BY `the business` BECAUSE "reg 529I(2): work still carried out 12 months after the last notice must be notified within 30 days after the 12-month period ends (tier G)"

-- regs 374(1), 375: the business must take all reasonable steps to obtain the report "as soon as practicable after the
-- monitoring is carried out", then give the worker a copy "as soon as practicable after the person obtains the report".
-- "As soon as practicable" is not a number of days, so no WITHIN is written.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Silica party` `Silica action`
`the health monitoring report duty` MEANS
    PARTY `the business`
    MUST  `obtain the health monitoring report`
    HENCE
        PARTY `the business`
        MUST  `give me a copy of the health monitoring report`
        LEST  BREACH BY `the business` BECAUSE "reg 375: the business must give the worker a copy of the health monitoring report as soon as practicable after obtaining it (tier E)"
    LEST  BREACH BY `the business` BECAUSE "reg 374(1): the business must take all reasonable steps to obtain the health monitoring report as soon as practicable (tier E)"
